# research/ is the formula-search project. Read plan.md first.
#
# Version control trade-offs, stated once:
#
#   data/  275 MB of raw OHLCV, regenerable in ~20 minutes with collect_bars.py.
#          It stays OUT of version control. It stays ON disk.
#
#   out/   Evidence. A formula's verdict is meaningless without the numbers and
#          the trusted universe it was computed on, so these files ARE tracked.
#          Per-round detail goes in out/<round-id>/ and history.md points at it.
#
#   src/   The harness is a hand-off contract, so it is tracked too. The repo
#          root .gitignore has a bare `src/` rule intended for the Python
#          package layout; it would silently swallow this directory.
#
# Ordering matters: the re-includes below MUST come before the ignore rules.
# A negation placed after an ignore re-includes everything it covers, which
# would pull __pycache__ and .DS_Store back in.

!src/
!src/**

data/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# The repo root ignores a bare `*.csv` (raw data dumps). A round's result
# tables are EVIDENCE, not raw data: plan.md 6.3 requires them in version
# control so a verdict can be audited against the numbers behind it.
!out/**/*.csv

# Scratch written by probing / throwaway scripts during a round. Never evidence.
_scratch/
src/_*.py
src/probe_*.py

# Per-ticker bar files from the Tiingo pull: tens of thousands of small gz
# files. The panel parquet built from them IS tracked (it is the evidence);
# the raw per-ticker shards are an intermediate, regenerable from the fetch.
out/**/tiingo/bars/
